{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/875213-how-does-long-road-to-heaven-work-out","id":875213,"title":"How does Long Road to Heaven Work out?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-26T20:44:44-07:00","id":875213,"title":"How does Long Road to Heaven Work out?","content":"For those who have run it, how does it work out? In particular a narrative sense?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T23:50:06-07:00","id":875367,"title":"","content":"For a mixed group it actually worked out pretty well for me. At least up to the middle of the demigod part. My group split up when some of us had to move away for work, so I can't say how it would have gone after that. But up until then it worked out really well. The trick was, after the initial Hero adventure, to throw in plenty of Yakuza and Shinobi trouble to plague the players as Kane targets them for foiling his schemes. I'd hit them where it hurt, and always keep Kane laughingly just out of their reach. By the time they realised in the second adventure that Kane was involved they were all raring to go after him.<br /> <br /> Mostly it also worked really well with lots of filler in Las Vegas. You can run through the adventure one scene at a time, and I've run it that way before, but I found that when I padded it out with some Las Vegas encounters that painted them in a heroic light they went into the whole thing feeling more like the Magnificent Seven (well OK, the Magnificent Four). Not even combat. Walking a drunken tourist back safe to her hotel room, the social guy talking down a pair of arguing honeymooners, and things like that to kind of establish their heroic cred before they were forced to prove it in front of a bunch of gods. Worked a treat and it caused them to feel protective of Las Vegas, so when the ship crashes into the strip they were fighting as much for the protection of their new home base as they were because they're Scions and that's just what you do.<br /> <br /> With lots of room to stretch their wings between plot-related drama, and some targetted minor side-quests to make them feel like heroes, it all played out smoothly. They were seriously fretting the loss of the Feather Shroud. It was a great time, all around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T10:50:17-07:00","id":875757,"title":"","content":"Cool. Thanks. Words from anyone else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}